.TH SDL_CompareCallback_r 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_CompareCallback_r \- A callback used with SDL sorting and binary search functions.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef int (SDLCALL *SDL_CompareCallback_r)(void *userdata, const void *a, const void *b);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I userdata
the
.BR userdata
pointer passed to the sort function\[char46]
.TP
.I a
a pointer to the first element being compared\[char46]
.TP
.I b
a pointer to the second element being compared\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns -1 if
.BR a
should be sorted before
.BR b ,
1 if
.BR b
should be sorted before
.BR a ,
0 if they are equal\[char46] If two elements are equal, their order in the sorted array is undefined\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This callback is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_qsort_r (3),
.BR SDL_bsearch_r (3)
